Read `.cursor/skills/debug-model-output/SKILL.md` before changing how the model is prompted, parsed
or sampled. The symptom in front of you probably has a recorded cause; check its table first.

- `enable_thinking: true`, the streamer's `skip_special_tokens: false` and the two-entry
  `eos_token_id` are all load-bearing. Dropping any one of them breaks tool calling silently.
- Behavioural claims need the harness at <http://localhost:5173/?eval>, not a few manual turns.
  Sampling is on, so a handful of runs cannot tell a real change from noise.
- `DEFAULT_STRATEGY` stays `baseline` until the harness says otherwise **on this model**. The
  reasoning-budget numbers in the comments come from a different, instruct-tuned one.
- Firmer tool-use instructions in `SYSTEM_PROMPT` were measured and made tool use worse. Leave it
  short.
- Every answer goes through `reviewAnswer` before it is returned, so one turn can generate twice.
  The checks stay deterministic and the correction states the fix; asking the model to grade itself
  is the thing that does not work.
